  "step_2": "For Lottery A: The 6000 Euros outcome has a probability of 0.1% (0.001). The adjusted probability is 0.1% + 10% = 10.1% (i.e., 0.101). The weighted outcome is 6000 * 0.101 = 606. The 0 Euro outcome is not considered in the sum as it contributes nothing. For Lottery B: The 3000 Euros outcome has a probability of 0.2% (0.002). The adjusted probability is 0.2% + 10% = 10.2% (i.e., 0.102). The weighted outcome is 3000 * 0.102 = 306. Comparing the weighted sums: Lottery A has 606, Lottery B has 306. Since 606 > 306, the decision reason prefers Lottery A.",
